DOCS_FRAGMENT("part:audit-repo", "<p class=\"lede partlede\">The audit of the repository. · source: <code>reference/AUDIT_2026-11-12_REPO.md</code></p><div class=\"sheetroot\" id=\"sheet-audit-repo\"><div class=\"tldr\"><div class=\"tldr-h\">In short</div><p>A read-only pass over the organisation of the repository, the replicability of the 1910\nplace-register pipeline, and the LaTeX tables. It answers three questions: (1) is the repo\norganised as its documentation says; (2) what from the register pipeline can go into a data\nreplication package; (3) which TeX tables exist and whether they are current.</p></div><nav class=\"toc\"><span>On this page</span><a href=\"#audit-repo-a-the-build-and-the-record\">A. The build and the record</a><a href=\"#audit-repo-b-against-the-code-amp-data-standards\">B. Against the Code &amp; Data Standards</a><a href=\"#audit-repo-c-documentation-drift\">C. Documentation drift</a><a href=\"#audit-repo-r-the-1910-register-in-a-replication-package\">R. The 1910 register in a replication package</a><a href=\"#audit-repo-t-latex-tables\">T. LaTeX tables</a><a href=\"#audit-repo-not-checked\">Not checked</a></nav>\n<p><strong>Method.</strong> Every claim below was measured on 2026-11-12 on Heavyhorse6, branch\n<code>heavyhorse6-2026-11-11</code>, HEAD <code>cddf6b0</code> (2026-11-11 21:47), with the working tree as other\nsessions left it (<code>git status --short</code>: 28 modified tracked files, 221 untracked entries\ncounting this report, most of them <code>reference/background/_evidence/parts/*</code>). Nothing was run that\nwrites to the repo or calls a model API. The checks used were <code>git ls-files</code> / <code>git status</code> /\n<code>git ls-files --eol</code>, reading the notebooks' JSON (sources <em>and</em> saved outputs), the QA gate\n<code>run_checks()</code> read-only against <code>data/final</code>, the full pytest suite, and in-memory\nrecomputation of every number the notebook-03 tables print. A full replay of notebook 03 into a\nscratch folder was refused by the session's permission layer, so table currency rests on the\nrecomputation (§T) rather than on a regenerated file.</p>\n<p><strong>Severity.</strong> <strong>[A]</strong> the build or the replication record is wrong or cannot be rebuilt ·\n<strong>[B]</strong> a standard (Gentzkow &amp; Shapiro, <code>CLAUDE.md</code> <em>Code &amp; Data Standards</em>) is not met ·\n<strong>[C]</strong> documentation drift. Each finding states its evidence, then a suggested fix. <strong>Nothing\nwas fixed.</strong> Several fixes touch files other sessions have open or <code>utils/lexikon_1910/</code>, which\nis frozen. Those are the author's to schedule.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"audit-repo-a-the-build-and-the-record\">A. The build and the record</h2>\n<h3 id=\"a1-the-code-that-builds-the-analysiss-register-is-not-in-git\">A1. The code that builds the analysis's register is not in git</h3>\n<p><code>data/final/register_rechecked/</code> is the register the analysis reads (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-200\">D-200</a>). It is built by\nnotebook 17 §9 from <code>utils/recheck/</code>. Git holds 2 of that package's 27 files (24 <code>.py</code>,\n3 <code>.html</code>):</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>git ls-files utils/recheck</code> returns <code>error_sample.py</code> and <code>error_sample_page.html</code> only.\n  <code>__init__.py</code>, <code>merge.py</code> (0.9.0), <code>register_rechecked.py</code> (0.7.0) and the 20 other modules\n  are untracked (<code>git status</code>: <code>??</code>).</li>\n<li><code>notebooks/17_recheck.ipynb</code> and <code>notebooks/15b_rulings_into_the_runs.ipynb</code> are untracked.</li>\n<li>16 of the 83 entries in <code>tests/</code> are untracked (15 test files and one <code>.tmp</code>). Among them\n  are the tests of most recheck modules (<code>test_author_carry.py</code>, <code>test_table_rows.py</code>,\n  <code>test_section_keys.py</code>, …); only <code>test_error_sample.py</code> is tracked.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>A clone of the repository therefore cannot rebuild <code>register_rechecked/</code>. The register's\ncorrection pass exists only in this Dropbox folder.</p>\n<p><strong>Fix.</strong> Commit <code>utils/recheck/</code>, notebooks 15b and 17 and the untracked tests, after deleting\nthe stray temp file in A6. This is the author's call: the branch is shared with live sessions.</p>\n<h3 id=\"a2-settlements_1910_geo-was-last-built-from-the-routes-register-before-the-rechecked-one-existed-in-its-current-form\">A2. <code>settlements_1910_geo</code> was last built from the route's register, before the rechecked one existed in its current form</h3>\n<p>There are two code paths to <code>data/final/geo/settlements_1910_geo</code>, and they disagree on which\nregister breaks name ties (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-155\">D-155</a>):</p>\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Writer</th>\n<th>Code</th>\n<th><code>register_dir</code></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>notebook 02 §3e</td>\n<td>cell 23</td>\n<td><code>DATA_FINAL / \"register_rechecked\"</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>notebook 15b §11</td>\n<td>cell 22</td>\n<td><code>DATA_FINAL / \"register\"</code> (the route's)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p>The file on disk came from 15b:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>On disk, <code>in_register_court</code> is non-null on <strong>15,045</strong> rows (12,800 True / 2,245 False).</li>\n<li>15b's saved output for cell 22 reads \"85.1% of <strong>15,045</strong> matched points\"; notebook 02's\n  saved output for cell 23 reads \"85.1% of <strong>15,043</strong>\".</li>\n<li>File times: <code>settlements_1910_geo.parquet</code> 2026-11-06 20:58, just after\n  <code>data/final/register/</code> (2026-11-06 20:42). <code>register_rechecked/</code> was rewritten\n  2026-11-11 20:42–20:44.</li>\n<li>Notebook 17 cell 36's saved output says it outright: <em>\"!! data/final/geo/settlements_1910_geo\n  is older than the register it breaks ties with: re-run notebook 02 §3e\"</em>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The crosswalk the analysis would use is therefore tied to the route's register, not to the\ncorrected one <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-200\">D-200</a> names. I did not measure how many tie-breaks differ. The two builds'\nmatched-point counts differ by 2 (15,045 against 15,043), which bounds the exposure only\nloosely.</p>\n<p><strong>Fix.</strong> Point 15b §11 at <code>register_rechecked</code> (or drop it and rely on notebook 02 §3e). Then\nre-run notebook 02 §3e after notebook 17 §9. The <code>crosswalk_stale()</code> warning should become a\nQA-gate check against <code>register_rechecked</code>, not only a printout.</p>\n<h3 id=\"a3-the-documented-run-order-is-wrong-the-build-is-interleaved-across-notebooks\">A3. The documented run order is wrong: the build is interleaved across notebooks</h3>\n<p><code>README.md</code> (<em>Reproducing</em>) says to run 01 → 02 → 03. The real dependency order is:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>notebook 02 §3a–§3c (districts, census, settlements)</li>\n<li>→ notebook 15 §18 (<code>data/final/register/</code>)</li>\n<li>→ notebook 15b (rulings)</li>\n<li>→ notebook 17 §9 (<code>register_rechecked/</code>)</li>\n<li>→ notebook 02 §3e (<code>settlements_1910_geo</code>, which reads <code>register_rechecked</code>, nb02 cell 23)</li>\n<li>→ notebook 03.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><code>REGISTER_VARIABLES.md</code> <em>Build order</em> records part of this, but neither <code>README.md</code> nor the\n<code>CLAUDE.md</code> tree does. That tree still heads <code>notebooks/</code> with \"THREE stage notebooks\". A\ntop-to-bottom run of notebook 02 on a clean <code>data/final</code> would call §3e before any register\nexists.</p>\n<p><strong>Fix.</strong> Write the order into <code>README.md</code> <em>Reproducing</em> and into the master-notebook plan. If\n§3e must run after the register, consider splitting it into its own stage.</p>\n<h3 id=\"a4-the-freeze-check-depends-on-line-endings-and-441-tracked-files-are-crlf-on-disk-but-lf-in-git\">A4. The freeze check depends on line endings, and 441 tracked files are CRLF on disk but LF in git</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><code>git ls-files --eol</code> gives <strong>441</strong> files <code>i/lf w/crlf</code>, 314 <code>i/lf w/lf</code> and 3 <code>w/mixed</code>.\n  By folder: 232 in <code>reference/background</code>, 69 in <code>reference/places</code>, 34 in\n  <code>utils/lexikon_1910</code>, 18 in <code>utils/parsing</code>, and others.</li>\n<li>The system gitconfig (<code>…/Git/etc/gitconfig</code>) sets <code>core.autocrlf=true</code>; <code>.git/config</code> sets\n  <code>false</code>; there is no <code>.gitattributes</code>.</li>\n<li>These files show as clean only because the index's stat cache matches. Once one is edited,\n  git compares bytes and the whole file differs. That is the cause of the\n  <code>reference/PIPELINE.md</code> and <code>reference/SITE_CHANGELOG.md</code> diffs: <code>git diff --stat</code> reports\n  2,437 and 3,077 lines; with <code>--ignore-cr-at-eol</code> the real change is 39 and 67 lines. HEAD's\n  copies are LF (<code>git show HEAD:… | file -</code>).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>The same mechanism reaches the frozen route.</strong> <code>run_frozen._digest</code> hashes raw bytes\n(<code>run_frozen.py:713</code>). I recomputed the 43 <code>code</code> digests in <code>output/frozen/cz_full/freeze/manifest.json</code>\nfrom HEAD's blobs. Every one matches, but only when <strong>21 files are written CRLF and 22 LF</strong>.\nA clone on Linux or macOS, or any checkout with <code>autocrlf=false</code>, would fail the freeze check\non those 21 files with no code change at all.</p>\n<p><strong>Fix.</strong> Do not touch <code>utils/lexikon_1910/</code>. Instead:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Pin endings with a <code>.gitattributes</code> that reproduces today's bytes per file, or ship the run\n  code as a byte-exact archive alongside the manifests (see §R).</li>\n<li>Renormalise the repo's prose and non-frozen code once, in its own commit, so edits stop\n  producing whole-file diffs.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"a5-a-frozen-route-file-carries-an-uncommitted-change-and-a-test-now-fails\">A5. A frozen-route file carries an uncommitted change, and a test now fails</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><code>utils/lexikon_1910/run_verify_test_b.py</code> is modified in the working tree: 1.12.0 → 1.13.0,\n  <code>unit_id</code> now appends 8 hex of a SHA-1 (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-189\">D-189</a>).</li>\n<li>Every 0.21.0 manifest (the four <code>*_full</code> runs and both <code>*_gold</code> runs) digests the\n  <strong>1.12.0</strong> file. Against the disk file the check reports exactly that one difference\n  (<code>!=disk 1 ['run_verify_test_b.py']</code>).</li>\n<li>pytest on the working tree: <strong>976 passed, 1 failed</strong>. The failure is\n  <code>tests/test_verify_test_b.py::test_unit_id_is_a_valid_custom_id</code>, which expects\n  <code>0019-a_-1-0</code> and gets <code>0019-a_-1-0-f39ddd49</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Notebook 15b's header already warns that notebook 15 §9 must not be re-run for this reason.</p>\n<p><strong>Fix.</strong> The author decides whether 1.13.0 is a route change, which needs a new freeze, or a\npost-run tool. Either way, update the test, and ship the <strong>1.12.0</strong> bytes as the code that\nproduced the runs.</p>\n<h3 id=\"a6-stray-files-where-they-can-be-committed-by-accident\">A6. Stray files where they can be committed by accident</h3>\n<p>These are untracked and not ignored:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>tests/test_matice.py.tmp.19732.4bea061f1cd3</code> (2026-11-03)</li>\n<li><code>utils/recheck/blind_sample.py.tmp.4068.8dc332b3e199</code> (2026-11-09)</li>\n<li><code>notebooks/archive/05_ocr_model_bakeoff (Heavyhorse6's conflicted copy 2026-08-14).ipynb</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p>The conflicted copy is not a duplicate: 33 cells against the tracked file's 19, and all 19\nshared positions differ.</p>\n<p><strong>Fix.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Delete the two <code>.tmp.*</code> files once their writers are confirmed dead.</li>\n<li>Diff the conflicted copy against <code>05_ocr_model_bakeoff.ipynb</code>, keep whichever is wanted, and\n  delete the other.</li>\n<li>Add <code>*.tmp.*</code> to <code>.gitignore</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"audit-repo-b-against-the-code-amp-data-standards\">B. Against the <em>Code &amp; Data Standards</em></h2>\n<h3 id=\"b1-the-qa-gate-passes-but-not-at-the-size-the-docs-say\">B1. The QA gate passes, but not at the size the docs say</h3>\n<p>Running <code>run_checks()</code> read-only on today's <code>data/final</code> gives:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>151 checks</strong> (140 hard, 11 soft).</li>\n<li><strong>0 hard failures.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>2 soft failures</strong>: \"Register: municipalities with institutions have a table row (511\n  without)\" and \"Register (rechecked): … (1 without)\".</li>\n</ul>\n<p><code>CLAUDE.md:123</code> still says <em>v1.12.0, 107 checks</em>; the module is 1.19.0\n(<code>utils/validation/data_checks.py:48</code>). <code>reference/VALIDATION.md:55</code> says the same.</p>\n<p><strong>Fix.</strong> Have the docs site render the count, or update the two lines.</p>\n<h3 id=\"b2-the-core-person-parsers-have-no-unit-tests\">B2. The core person parsers have no unit tests</h3>\n<p>No file in <code>tests/</code> imports any of these: <code>dates</code>, <code>education</code>, <code>exit_codes</code>, <code>ranks</code>,\n<code>occupations</code>, <code>affiliations</code>, <code>units</code>, <code>theater</code>, <code>habsburg</code>, <code>schema</code>, <code>census</code>, <code>clean</code>,\nor <code>utils/linkage.py</code>.</p>\n<p>Parsing modules the tests do import: <code>amateur_theatre*</code>, <code>geonames</code>, <code>lexikon</code>, <code>locative</code>,\n<code>matice</code>, <code>prng</code>, <code>records_geo</code>, <code>ruian</code>, <code>spatial</code>, <code>vua_courts</code>. All 977 tests cover the\nregister, recheck, theatre, matice and geography code. The modules that build every\nanalysis variable (rank reset, exit codes, HISCO, the linkage) are guarded only by the QA\ngate's invariants on the built data.</p>\n<p><strong>Fix.</strong> Add small known-answer tests for at least <code>exit_codes</code>, <code>ranks.rank_reset</code>,\n<code>education</code>, <code>dates</code> and <code>linkage.find_overlap</code>. The audit-2026-09-22 cases (A1–A8) are\nready-made fixtures.</p>\n<h3 id=\"b3-keys-unique-where-measured-but-not-declared-everywhere\">B3. Keys: unique where measured, but not declared everywhere</h3>\n<p><strong>Asserted in the gate:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>legion_id</code>, <code>vua_id</code> (<code>data_checks.py:163–165</code>)</li>\n<li><code>settlements_1910.settlement_id</code></li>\n<li>every register table via <code>reg.TABLE_KEYS</code></li>\n<li><code>register_place_types</code></li>\n<li>the RÚIAN / Geonames / PRNG / vanished tables and <code>settlements_1910_geo</code></li>\n<li>one-to-one <code>overlap_matches</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Not asserted.</strong> I measured these myself:</p>\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Table</th>\n<th>Rows</th>\n<th>Key that holds</th>\n<th>Note</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>census/census_okres_1910</code></td>\n<td>158</td>\n<td><code>okres_id</code> unique, 0 null</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>census/census_okres_1910_pooled</code></td>\n<td>148</td>\n<td><code>census_okres_id</code> unique, 0 null</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>census/census_hu_jaras_1910</code></td>\n<td>192</td>\n<td><code>unit_id</code> unique, 0 null</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>geo/districts_1910</code></td>\n<td>339</td>\n<td><code>court_id</code> unique, 0 null</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>geo/districts_hu_1910</code></td>\n<td>192</td>\n<td><code>unit_id</code> unique, 0 null</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>geo/okres_census_crosswalk</code></td>\n<td>158</td>\n<td><code>okres_id</code> unique</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>geo/okres_centroids_1910</code></td>\n<td>156</td>\n<td><code>okres_id</code> unique</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>analysis/*_census_1910</code>, <code>*_census_hu_1910</code> (4)</td>\n<td>132,993 / 186,192</td>\n<td><code>legion_id</code> / <code>vua_id</code> unique</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>geo/settlements_hu_1910</code></td>\n<td>3,511</td>\n<td><strong>no id column</strong></td>\n<td><code>(obec_sk, okres_sk)</code> has 0 duplicates; <code>unit_id</code> is the járás (57 null, not unique)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>geo/settlement_aliases_1910</code></td>\n<td>10,213</td>\n<td><strong>none</strong></td>\n<td>columns <code>cs_name, viz_target, viz_okres</code>; <strong>4 exact duplicate rows</strong>; 224 duplicates on <code>(cs_name, viz_okres)</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>data_dictionary.csv</code></td>\n<td>—</td>\n<td>not checked</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Fix.</strong> Add these tables to the gate's key checks, give <code>settlements_hu_1910</code> an id, and\ndeduplicate the alias table.</p>\n<h3 id=\"b4-outputs-that-nothing-rebuilds\">B4. Outputs that nothing rebuilds</h3>\n<p>I searched <code>utils/</code> and all notebooks for each item's name (<code>grep -rlF</code>):</p>\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Size</th>\n<th>Date</th>\n<th>Status</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>output/tables/sample/</code> (3 <code>.tex</code> + 3 <code>.csv</code>)</td>\n<td>3 KB</td>\n<td>2026-07-14</td>\n<td>no writer; already open in <code>ROADMAP.md:29</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>output/font_specimen.html</code></td>\n<td>1.2 MB</td>\n<td>2026-09-02</td>\n<td>no writer</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>output/recheck/unnumbered_rows_examples.png</code></td>\n<td>1.65 MB</td>\n<td>2026-11-11</td>\n<td>no writer (the \"leftover image\" lead: confirmed)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>output/recheck_review/REVIEW_2026-11-09.md</code></td>\n<td>39 KB</td>\n<td>2026-11-09</td>\n<td>an <em>authored</em> review, cited by <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-198\">D-198</a> and <code>RECHECK.md</code>, but stored in gitignored <code>output/</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Analysis.zip</code> (repo root, gitignored)</td>\n<td>25.2 MB</td>\n<td>2026-05-20</td>\n<td>no reference anywhere</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>output/publish/legions-docs/</code></td>\n<td>646 MB</td>\n<td>—</td>\n<td>a nested git repo assembled by hand (README: \"can be assembled\")</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Fix.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Delete the sample tables, the specimen and the PNG, or write a cell that rebuilds them.</li>\n<li>Move <code>REVIEW_2026-11-09.md</code> into <code>reference/</code> so it is tracked, as <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-198\">D-198</a> cites it.</li>\n<li>Decide what <code>Analysis.zip</code> is.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"b5-csv-and-parquet-mirrors-agree-their-file-times-do-not-prove-staleness\">B5. CSV and parquet mirrors agree; their file times do not prove staleness</h3>\n<p>Several CSV mirrors in <code>data/final</code> are older than their parquet twins. Examples:\n<code>census_hu_jaras_1910.csv</code> (2026-07-15) against its <code>.parquet</code> (2026-11-05), and\n<code>districts_hu_1910.csv</code> (2026-08-01). Notebook 02 writes both formats in the same cell\n(lines 203–316 of its code). I compared content over 9 pairs: districts ×2, census ×3,\nsettlements ×2 and both person files (132,993 × 219 and 186,192 × 102), with NA and number\nformatting normalised. There are <strong>0 differing cells</strong>.</p>\n<p>The CSVs are current. Notebook 03's saved outputs write to <code>C:\\Users\\tomas\\…</code>, so notebook 03\nlast ran on the other machine. A file time on this machine is consistent with \"the last time\nthe bytes changed\". Do not read it as \"the last run\".</p>\n<p>No fix needed; recorded so nobody \"fixes\" it.</p>\n<h3 id=\"b6-the-saved-notebook-state-is-not-a-clean-top-to-bottom-run\">B6. The saved notebook state is not a clean top-to-bottom run</h3>\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Notebook</th>\n<th>Saved state</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>01</td>\n<td>execution counts non-monotonic (…10, 4, …, 2, …); 9 of 17 code cells unexecuted</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>02, 03, 15b</td>\n<td>clean 1…n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>15</td>\n<td>an <strong>error output</strong> in cell 50 (<code>KeyError: 'certification_superseded_round1'</code>); 3 code cells unexecuted</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>16</td>\n<td>never executed (expected: SPEND off)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>17</td>\n<td>last code cell <code>[3]</code> after <code>[21]</code>; 4 code cells unexecuted</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p>The saved outputs also carry <strong>93 lines of absolute machine paths with user names</strong>: 61 in\nnotebook 03 (<code>C:\\Users\\tomas\\…</code>), 28 in 15, 3 in 01 and 1 in 02.</p>\n<p><strong>Fix.</strong> Before any notebook is shipped or made public, clear outputs or re-run it clean.</p>\n<h3 id=\"b7-absolute-paths-and-machine-bound-artefacts\">B7. Absolute paths and machine-bound artefacts</h3>\n<p><strong>Code cells.</strong> None hold an absolute path.</p>\n<p><strong>Code files:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>utils/docs/build_fonts.py:19</code>: <code>Path.home() / \"AppData/Local/Programs/MiKTeX/…\"</code>, a\n  Windows MiKTeX default.</li>\n<li><code>tests/test_batch_wait.py:93</code>: this machine's repo path, inside a monkeypatch.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Data artefacts:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The reader queues live <strong>outside the repo and outside Dropbox</strong>, in\n  <code>D:\\Users_Data\\thaufer\\lexikon_1910_queues</code> (303 MB; <code>run_frozen.queue_root()</code>,\n  <code>run_frozen.py:440–453</code>).</li>\n<li>Every queue line stores an absolute <code>cache_dir</code> (<code>D:\\Users_Data\\thaufer\\Dropbox\\…</code>).</li>\n<li>That folder is the <strong>only</strong> copy of the raw Gemini batch results (<code>*.results.jsonl</code>). Their\n  parsed form is in the Dropbox cache (§R). I did not check whether any backup covers\n  <code>D:\\Users_Data\\thaufer</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Fix.</strong> Back up <code>lexikon_1910_queues</code> before anything else on this list.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"audit-repo-c-documentation-drift\">C. Documentation drift</h2>\n<h3 id=\"c1-the-claudemd-tree-omits-much-of-what-is-on-disk\">C1. The <code>CLAUDE.md</code> tree omits much of what is on disk</h3>\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>On disk, not in the tree</th>\n<th>Evidence</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>notebooks/17_recheck.ipynb</code></td>\n<td>the tree lists 01, 02, 03, 15, 15b, 16, <code>archive/</code>; prose mentions \"notebook 17 §9\" once (line 42)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>utils/recheck/</code> (24 <code>.py</code> + 3 <code>.html</code>)</td>\n<td>not mentioned in <code>CLAUDE.md</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>tests/</code> (83 entries, 977 tests)</td>\n<td>only the word \"pytest\" (line 261)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>utils/docs/</code> (<code>build_docs.py</code>, <code>build_fonts.py</code>)</td>\n<td>not in the tree; <code>README.md</code> mentions <code>build_docs.py</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>10 parsing modules</td>\n<td><code>amateur_theatre</code>, <code>amateur_theatre_consensus</code>, <code>amateur_theatre_model</code>, <code>geonames</code>, <code>locative</code>, <code>matice</code>, <code>prng</code>, <code>ruian</code>, <code>vanished</code>, <code>vua_courts</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>7 of 8 validation scripts</td>\n<td>the tree shows <code>data_checks.py</code> only; also <code>build_validation_workbook</code>, <code>check_offices_coverage</code>, <code>check_ostafin_silesia</code>, <code>lexikon_population</code>, <code>run_completeness</code>, <code>score_sealed_retest</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>9 of 11 scraping scripts</td>\n<td>the tree shows <code>scraper_csol.py</code>, <code>scraper_vuapraha.py</code>; also <code>fetch_vua_courts</code>, <code>progress</code>, <code>run_lexicon_downloads</code>, <code>run_matice_downloads</code>, <code>run_oeulk_downloads</code>, <code>scraper_amaterskedivadlo</code>, <code>scraper_kramerius</code>, <code>scraper_kramerius7</code>, <code>scraper_verlustlisten</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>11 <code>reference/*.md</code></td>\n<td><code>AUDIT_2026-10-24</code>, <code>AUDIT_2026-11-11_THEATRE</code>, <code>INTENSITY_MAPS</code>, <code>LEXIKON_1910</code>, <code>LEXIKON_1910_ROUTE</code>, <code>MATICE_MEASURE</code>, <code>OVERVIEW</code>, <code>RECHECK</code>, <code>REGISTER_VARIABLES</code>, <code>SYMBOL_ACCURACY_PLAN</code>, <code>VALIDATION_EDUCATION</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>data/final/register/</code>, <code>register_rechecked/</code></td>\n<td>described in the data section, missing from the tree's <code>data/</code> line</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>reading_corpus/</code>, <code>requirements.lock.txt</code></td>\n<td>only <code>.gitignore</code> describes <code>reading_corpus/</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p>The four leads given for this audit:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>utils/recheck/</code> and <code>tests/</code> missing from the tree: <strong>confirmed</strong>.</li>\n<li>Notebooks 15b and 17 untracked: <strong>confirmed</strong> (A1).</li>\n<li>The Dropbox conflicted copy exists: <strong>confirmed</strong>, and it differs from the original (A6).</li>\n<li>CRLF whole-file diffs on <code>PIPELINE.md</code> and <code>SITE_CHANGELOG.md</code>: <strong>confirmed</strong>, and it is\n  repo-wide (A4).</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"c2-versions-quoted-in-current-state-docs\">C2. Versions quoted in current-state docs</h3>\n<p>A scan of <code>CLAUDE.md</code> matched quoted versions for 26 modules; 24 agree with the module's\n<code>__version__</code>, counting <code>1.4</code> as matching <code>1.4.x</code>. The three that disagree (the third,\n<code>data_checks</code>, was found by hand):</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>lexikon</code> 1.5 → <strong>1.7.0</strong></li>\n<li><code>records_geo</code> 1.8 → <strong>1.9.0</strong></li>\n<li><code>data_checks</code> v1.12.0 → <strong>1.19.0</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><code>linkage.py</code> 1.3.0 matches (<code>utils/linkage.py:79</code>).</p>\n<p><code>RECHECK.md</code> quotes <code>both_ways</code> 0.1.1/0.1.2, <code>editions_check</code> 0.1.2/0.1.3, <code>opus_pass</code> 0.2.1\nand <code>unasked</code> 0.4.1. The modules are now 0.1.3, 0.1.4, 0.2.2 and 0.4.2. These quotes sit in\ndated narrative (\"<code>unasked</code> 0.4.1 adds…\"), so they are history, not drift.</p>\n<p>The same holds for the old versions in <code>ROADMAP.md</code>, <code>OCCUPATION_CODING.md</code> and\n<code>DECISIONS.md</code>. One exception is current-state text: <code>VALIDATION.md:55</code> (<code>data_checks</code>\n1.12.0, B1).</p>\n<p><strong>Modules without <code>__version__</code></strong> (the stated module convention), 15 in all:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>scraping/scraper_csol.py</code>, <code>scraping/scraper_vuapraha.py</code></li>\n<li><code>docs/build_docs.py</code></li>\n<li><code>validation/build_validation_workbook.py</code></li>\n<li><code>reference_tools/units/build_unit_authority.py</code>, <code>reference_tools/units/run_vua_courts_pilot.py</code></li>\n<li>6 in <code>reference_tools/places</code></li>\n<li>2 in <code>reference_tools/background</code></li>\n<li><code>recheck/__init__.py</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"c3-stale-facts-in-the-docs\">C3. Stale facts in the docs</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><code>CLAUDE.md</code> puts the linkage crosswalk at <code>data/final/overlap_matches.csv</code>. It is at\n  <code>data/final/persons/overlap_matches.csv</code>.</li>\n<li><code>CLAUDE.md</code> and <code>DATA_SOURCES.md:30</code> give the <a class=\"gl\" href=\"#gl-vúa-cs\" data-gl=\"vúa\">VÚA</a> scrape as <strong>186,191</strong> records. Both\n  <code>data/raw/habsburg/habsburg_fallen.csv</code> and <code>habsburg_clean</code> have <strong>186,192</strong> rows.</li>\n<li><code>CLAUDE.md:219</code> says \"notebooks 02 and 03 re-run 2026-09-23 — <code>data/final</code>, the 28 figures\n  and the 14 LaTeX tables are current\". In fact the person files were rewritten 2026-11-05\n  23:33, and one table is now stale (§T).</li>\n<li><code>DATA_SOURCES.md:52</code> (#7a, the Czech register) says <em>\"In progress, nothing in <code>data/</code>\n  derives from it yet\"</em>. <code>data/final/register/</code> and <code>register_rechecked/</code> derive from it.</li>\n<li><code>DATA_SOURCES.md</code> has rows for the Czech (#7a) and German Böhmen (#7b) volumes only. The\n  Mähren and Schlesien volumes, both read in full (<code>output/frozen/de-moravia_full</code>,\n  <code>de-silesia_full</code>), appear only in <code>library/SOURCES.md:73–74</code>.</li>\n<li>The <code>CLAUDE.md</code> <em>Known Data Issues</em> text quotes <code>ranks</code> 1.4.1; the module is 1.4.3. Minor.</li>\n<li><code>README.md</code> still describes a three-notebook pipeline. It lists 2 of 11 scrapers, calls\n  <code>validation/</code> a \"human-validation workbook builder\", never mentions the register, and its\n  <em>Status</em> ends at the 2026-09-23 re-run.</li>\n<li><code>.gitignore</code>'s secrets comment points to <code>utils/parsing/lexikon_1910_pages.py</code>. The file is\n  <code>utils/lexikon_1910/lexikon_1910_pages.py</code>.</li>\n<li><code>ROADMAP.md</code> and <code>SYMBOL_ACCURACY_PLAN.md</code> cite notebooks 05–14 at <code>notebooks/</code>. They are\n  in <code>notebooks/archive/</code>. In <code>DECISIONS.md</code> the same paths are dated history, so correct as\n  written.</li>\n<li><code>PIPELINE.md</code> and <code>VALIDATION_EDUCATION.md</code> cite <code>education_gold/NAVOD.md</code>. The file is at\n  <code>reference/education/education_gold/NAVOD.md</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Checked and sound.</strong> Every <code>.py</code> / <code>.ipynb</code> / <code>.md</code> path named in <code>CLAUDE.md</code>, <code>README.md</code>\nand the 26 <code>reference/*.md</code> resolves to an existing file, apart from glob patterns and the\nmoved paths listed above. 8,786 files were indexed across <code>utils/</code>, <code>notebooks/</code>,\n<code>reference/</code>, <code>tests/</code>, <code>library/</code> and <code>data/final/</code>. Every file in <code>data/final</code> has a writer\nin notebook 02, 15, 15b or 17.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"audit-repo-r-the-1910-register-in-a-replication-package\">R. The 1910 register in a replication package</h2>\n<h3 id=\"what-the-record-is\">What the record is</h3>\n<p><strong>The run folders.</strong> Each frozen run folder (<code>output/frozen/&lt;edition&gt;_&lt;pages&gt;/</code>) holds:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>freeze/manifest.json</code>: runner version; reader labels; module versions; <strong>sha256-16\n  digests</strong> of 13 curated inputs and of every route module (43 files, plus 10 recorded but not\n  compared); pixel digests of the two images; package versions (<code>anthropic</code> 1.4.0,\n  <code>google-genai</code> 2.22.0, <code>torch</code> 2.14.1+cu130, …); host <code>heavyhorse6</code>.</li>\n<li><code>reads/</code>: completion markers.</li>\n<li><code>opus/</code>: requests, <code>answers_raw.csv</code>, <code>usage.csv</code>, <code>batches.json</code>.</li>\n<li><code>ledger/</code>, <code>final_*.csv</code>, <code>review/</code>, and the validation sheets.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>There are 13 manifests.</p>\n<p><strong>Model ids.</strong> Recorded per queue line and per cache record: <code>gemini-3.8-flash</code>,\n<code>claude-haiku-5-5</code>, and <code>claude-opus-5-5</code> (effort <code>low</code>, <code>opus/batches.json</code>). These are\nprovider <strong>aliases</strong>, not dated snapshots. The Gemini raw results also carry\n<code>response.modelVersion = gemini-3.8-flash</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Dates.</strong> Each cache record has an <code>at</code> timestamp; batch records have <code>submitted</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Where the model replies are:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>output/lexikon_1910_pilot/bakeoff/heavyhorse6/crop_cache/</code> (15.5 MB, 19,026 files) and\n  <code>…/table_cache/</code> (15.4 MB, 16,202 files). The German <code>…/de/</code> cache was not measured.</li>\n<li>One JSON record per crop: <code>{lines, usage, slot, kind, model, at, batched}</code>\n  (<code>reader_batches._write_cache</code>, <code>reader_batches.py:174</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>For Claude readers only the parsed payload is kept.</strong> <code>_parse_claude</code> stores\n  <code>json.loads(text)[payload_key]</code> (<code>reader_batches.py:580–596</code>). The verbatim text is not\n  kept, and a reply that fails to parse is discarded and read live. Anthropic batch results\n  are not retained by the provider long-term, so the verbatim Claude replies are unrecoverable.</li>\n<li><strong>For Gemini the raw batch results survive</strong>, in <code>lexikon_1910_queues/*.results.jsonl</code>\n  (B7).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Prompts</strong> are code, in <code>utils/lexikon_1910/*.py</code>, held by the manifests' digests. HEAD\nreproduces all 43 <code>cz_full</code> code digests when line endings are restored (A4).</p>\n<p><strong><code>reference/background/_evidence/digests/</code></strong> (13 files, untracked) holds the\n<em>reading-pass</em> digests, not the register's. The register's code is held by the manifests\nabove.</p>\n<h3 id=\"two-kinds-of-reproduction\">Two kinds of reproduction</h3>\n<p><strong>(I) Reproduce the analysis from <code>data/final</code>.</strong> This is deterministic and needs no API:\nnotebook 03, the estimation stage still to come, and the register tables. The register part\nof <code>data/final</code> describes 1910 places and institutions, not persons, so it can ship:</p>\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Table set</th>\n<th>Parquet</th>\n<th>CSV</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>register_rechecked/</code></td>\n<td>≈ 5.8 MB</td>\n<td>≈ 43.7 MB</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>(II) Reproduce the reading of the register.</strong> Re-calling the APIs is not replication. The\nmodel aliases move and retire, output is non-deterministic, batch pricing and quotas change,\nand it costs money. Under AEA Data Editor practice, as I understand it (the policy text was\nnot re-read for this audit), the replicable unit for an LLM step is:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>the code and prompts;</li>\n<li>model identifiers, dates and parameters;</li>\n<li>the <strong>archived outputs</strong>;</li>\n<li>code that rebuilds every downstream table <em>from those outputs</em>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Here that means:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>replaying notebook 15 §§12/14/16/18 → 15b → 17 §9 from the cached replies with\n  <code>SPEND=False</code>;</li>\n<li>shipping the gold, certification and error-sample evidence that bounds the reading's\n  accuracy (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-127\">D-127</a>, <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-226\">D-226</a>).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>I did <strong>not</strong> verify that a cache-only replay runs end to end on a clean machine. That is the\ncheck to run before a package is assembled.</p>\n<h3 id=\"what-to-ship\">What to ship</h3>\n<p>Sizes are measured on 2026-11-12. \"Text\" means everything except <code>.png</code>/<code>.jpg</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Ship?</th>\n<th>Why</th>\n<th>Size</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Route code <code>utils/lexikon_1910/*.py</code> at the bytes the freeze digests (1.12.0 <code>run_verify_test_b.py</code>; CRLF/LF as in A4)</td>\n<td><strong>Yes</strong></td>\n<td>The prompts and the parser are the method; the digests must verify</td>\n<td>5.9 MB tracked <code>utils/</code> in all</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Recheck code <code>utils/recheck/</code>, notebooks 15, 15b, 17</td>\n<td><strong>Yes</strong>, once committed (A1)</td>\n<td>They build <code>register_rechecked/</code></td>\n<td>&lt; 1 MB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>13 <code>freeze/manifest.json</code></td>\n<td><strong>Yes</strong></td>\n<td>Model ids, versions, package versions, input and code digests</td>\n<td>&lt; 0.1 MB each</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Model replies: <code>crop_cache/</code>, <code>table_cache/</code>, <code>de/</code></td>\n<td><strong>Yes</strong></td>\n<td>The archived outputs; replay reads them instead of the API</td>\n<td>≈ 31 MB + <code>de/</code> (not measured)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Raw Gemini batch results <code>lexikon_1910_queues/*.results.jsonl</code> + <code>*.batches.json</code></td>\n<td><strong>Yes</strong> (optional, as the verbatim record)</td>\n<td>The only verbatim replies kept; single copy today (B7)</td>\n<td>≤ 303 MB with queues</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Request queues <code>*.queue.jsonl</code></td>\n<td>Optional</td>\n<td>They name each request's key and model, but carry absolute <code>cache_dir</code> paths (B7)</td>\n<td>in the 303 MB above</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Full-run folders, <strong>text part</strong> (<code>cz/de-bohemia/de-moravia/de-silesia_full</code>)</td>\n<td><strong>Yes</strong></td>\n<td>Ledgers, Opus answers and usage, final inventories, review records</td>\n<td>132.1 + 187.7 + 44.7 + 13.3 = <strong>377.8 MB</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Full-run folders, <strong>images</strong></td>\n<td><strong>No</strong></td>\n<td>Page and mark crops cut from the scans by the code. Pixel digests exist for two components only; bit-identical regeneration not verified</td>\n<td>8.31 + 19.56 + 6.10 + 1.66 = <strong>35.6 GB</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Gold runs (text) / certification runs (text)</td>\n<td><strong>Yes</strong></td>\n<td>Calibration and the sealed certification behind <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-127\">D-127</a></td>\n<td>gold 432.8 + 109.9 MB; certification 1.7 + 1.1 + 0.8 + 0.9 + 0.1 MB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>*_superseded_round1</code>, <code>rehearsal_*</code>, <code>gemini_batch_check</code>, <code>lexikon_1910_pilot/</code> bake-off, <code>glyph_*</code>, <code>verify_test_b*</code>, <code>token_review</code>, <code>lexikon_1910_v2</code></td>\n<td><strong>No</strong> (archive separately if wanted), except the reply caches inside <code>lexikon_1910_pilot/</code> listed above</td>\n<td>Development history; superseded by the frozen route. Describe in the README</td>\n<td>≈ 2.5 GB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Human rulings <code>output/review_readback/</code> (each with <code>SOURCE.txt</code>)</td>\n<td><strong>Yes</strong></td>\n<td>Author rulings outrank the models and are data. ⚠ <code>SOURCE.txt</code> cites a private claude.ai artifact URL (e.g. <em>Czech Open Marks</em>), so the JSON is the record and the page is not reachable by a replicator; say so</td>\n<td>0.9 MB, 2,807 files</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Gold and certification transcriptions <code>reference/places/transcription_gold/</code> (<code>.md</code>, worksheets, keys)</td>\n<td><strong>Yes</strong></td>\n<td>The yardstick; already tracked</td>\n<td>1.3 MB tracked (64 files)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Gold page crops (<code>transcription_gold/**/*.png</code>)</td>\n<td><strong>No</strong></td>\n<td>Regenerable from the PDFs by <code>make_gold_worksheet*.py</code> (<code>.gitignore</code> comment)</td>\n<td>1.3 GB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sealed retest <code>output/frozen/sealed_retest/</code></td>\n<td><strong>Yes</strong></td>\n<td>Score files of the sealed half</td>\n<td>0.3 MB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Error sample (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-226\">D-226</a>): <code>utils/recheck/error_sample.py</code>, <code>reference/places/error_sample/error_sample_key.csv</code>, <code>output/review_readback/error_sample/</code> (rulings, reconcile), <code>output/recheck/error_sample/files_*.json</code></td>\n<td><strong>Yes</strong> — after the Mähren/Schlesien ruling now under way is final</td>\n<td>The blind precision/recall bounds</td>\n<td>key 64 KB; rest &lt; 1 MB (images in <code>img/</code>, <code>glyph/</code> not shipped)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>output/recheck/</code> text (changes, inventories, scores)</td>\n<td><strong>Yes</strong> for what §9 reads; the rest optional</td>\n<td>The correction pass's inputs</td>\n<td>140.2 MB text; images 5.73 GB <strong>not</strong> shipped</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Register scans: NDK Czech, UBW Böhmen and Mähren, MSVK Schlesien PDFs</td>\n<td><strong>No</strong> — cite persistent ids</td>\n<td>Public domain by age (1915–1918 state printing; NDK pages reported <em>public</em>, <code>DATA_SOURCES.md:52</code>), but large and stably hosted. Give the urn/uuid from <code>library/SOURCES.md:72–75</code> and the sha256 of each file</td>\n<td>3,340 + 676 + 340 + 111 MB = <strong>4.47 GB</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>data/final/register_rechecked/</code></td>\n<td><strong>Yes</strong></td>\n<td>The analysis's register; place-level, no persons</td>\n<td>≈ 5.8 MB parquet</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>.secrets/</code>, notebook outputs with machine paths</td>\n<td><strong>Never</strong> / strip</td>\n<td>Keys; user names in paths (B6)</td>\n<td>—</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h3 id=\"licences-and-redistribution-source-by-source\">Licences and redistribution, source by source</h3>\n<p>Claims marked <em>DATA_SOURCES</em> are the repo's own record. I did not re-check any provider's\nterms online. The legal reading in the first two rows is mine, not advice.</p>\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Source (<code>CLAUDE.md</code> data table)</th>\n<th>Recorded terms</th>\n<th>Ship in a public package?</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"gl\" href=\"#gl-csol-cz-cs\" data-gl=\"csol.cz\">csol.cz</a> legionnaire records (scraped)</td>\n<td>§90 zákon 121/2000 (research extraction) + GDPR Art. 89</td>\n<td><strong>No.</strong> §90 permits extraction for research, not redistribution; the database maker's right stays with ČsOL/VÚA, and the rows carry names and birth dates. Ship the scraper, the data dictionary and access instructions; deposit restricted-access only with the maker's consent</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>VÚA fallen soldiers (scraped)</td>\n<td>as above</td>\n<td><strong>No</strong>, same reasoning</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"gl\" href=\"#gl-mpidr-en\" data-gl=\"mpidr\">MPIDR</a> / Rumpler-Seger 1910 GIS (tracked in <code>reference/places/mpidr/</code>)</td>\n<td>citation required (<code>DATA_SOURCES.md</code> §5); <strong>no licence stated</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Check first.</strong> Distributed via MOSAIC/IPUMS, whose terms may bar redistribution. Until settled, point to the source</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Cisleithanian census workbooks (<code>data/raw/census/</code>)</td>\n<td>citation (Rumpler &amp; Seger 2010)</td>\n<td>Pointer; derived okres tables can ship once the terms are checked</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"gl\" href=\"#gl-gista-hungarorum-hu\" data-gl=\"gista hungarorum\">GISta Hungarorum</a></td>\n<td><strong>CC BY-NC</strong> (<code>DATA_SOURCES.md:90</code>)</td>\n<td>Derived tables yes, with attribution, if the package licence allows NC content; else pointer</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>ČSÚ <em><a class=\"gl\" href=\"#gl-historický-lexikon-obcí-cs\" data-gl=\"historický lexikon obcí\">Historický lexikon obcí</a></em></td>\n<td>not stated beyond provider</td>\n<td>Pointer; derived <code>settlements_1910</code> as derived facts</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"gl\" href=\"#gl-majo-2012-sk\" data-gl=\"majo 2012\">Majo 2012</a> (ŠÚSR)</td>\n<td>not stated</td>\n<td>Pointer</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Wikidata</td>\n<td>CC0</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>RÚIAN, Geonames (ČÚZK)</td>\n<td>CC-BY 4.0</td>\n<td>Yes, with <em>Zdroj: ČÚZK</em></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>PRNG (GUGiK)</td>\n<td>free for any use</td>\n<td>Yes, cited</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>HISCO / HSN</td>\n<td><strong>CC-BY-SA 4.0</strong></td>\n<td>Yes; <code>hisco_authority.csv</code> inherits CC-BY-SA (<code>reference/occupations/SOURCE_LICENCE.txt</code>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fidler 2025 epub</td>\n<td>in copyright</td>\n<td><strong>No</strong> epub; <code>unit_authority.csv</code> is facts only (<code>DATA_SOURCES.md:323</code>); validation only</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"gl\" href=\"#gl-ehnl-1934-de\" data-gl=\"ehnl 1934\">Ehnl 1934</a>, <em>Schematismus</em></td>\n<td>public domain by age</td>\n<td>Yes (derived CSVs); scans by pointer</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MOSAIC Vienna Database</td>\n<td><strong>no redistribution grant</strong> (<code>DATA_SOURCES.md:216–220</code>)</td>\n<td><strong>No</strong>; the <code>.sav</code> stays out; ship the check script and the published aggregates</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CZ-ISCO (ČSÚ), ILO ISCO-08</td>\n<td>ČSÚ reuse with attribution; ILO volume not stated</td>\n<td><code>czisco_authority.csv</code> yes; ILO by pointer</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><em>Österreichische Statistik</em> XCIII/1</td>\n<td>public domain by age</td>\n<td>Pointer (ÖNB)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Ostafin et al. 2020</td>\n<td><strong>CC0</strong></td>\n<td>Yes (validation only)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Register volumes (#7a, #7b, Mähren, Schlesien)</td>\n<td>public domain by age; NDK pages \"public\"</td>\n<td>Pointer + sha256 (above)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"audit-repo-t-latex-tables\">T. LaTeX tables</h2>\n<p>There are <strong>19 <code>.tex</code> tables on disk</strong>, all under <code>output/tables/</code>. <code>tex/</code> and <code>paper/</code> hold\n4 <code>.tex</code> <em>documents</em> and no table. None of them <code>\\input</code>s a generated table;\n<code>tex/25-05-26-EDA/25-05-26-EDA.tex</code> includes 6 figures from <code>output/figures/</code>. The listing\nexcludes <code>output/publish/</code>, which was not searched.</p>\n<h3 id=\"notebook-03-14-tables-all-via-utilstableslatex_tablespy-120\">Notebook 03 (14 tables, all via <code>utils/tables/latex_tables.py</code> 1.2.0)</h3>\n<p>Checked by recomputing the printed numbers from today's <code>data/final</code> (person files written\n2026-11-05 23:33):</p>\n<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>#</th>\n<th>File (<code>output/tables/…</code>)</th>\n<th>Cell</th>\n<th>Function</th>\n<th>mtime</th>\n<th>Against today's <code>data/final</code></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td><code>descriptives/data_quality/exit_codes.tex</code></td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td><code>exit_code_table</code></td>\n<td>2026-07-30</td>\n<td><strong>current</strong>: all 11 codes and \"no code\" 30,770 equal</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td><code>descriptives/theater/theater_summary.tex</code></td>\n<td>5</td>\n<td><code>df_to_latex</code></td>\n<td>2026-09-23</td>\n<td><strong>current</strong>: n and deserted per theatre equal</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td><code>descriptives/rank/rank_reset_summary.tex</code></td>\n<td>11</td>\n<td><code>df_to_latex</code></td>\n<td>2026-09-23</td>\n<td><strong>current</strong>: 85,698 / 91,561 / 85,698, shares, means, medians equal</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td><code>descriptives/occupation/occupation_hisclass_composition.tex</code></td>\n<td>13</td>\n<td><code>df_to_latex</code></td>\n<td>2026-09-23</td>\n<td><strong>current</strong> on N per class (13 rows); desertion column not recomputed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>5</td>\n<td><code>descriptives/occupation/desertion_by_hisclass.tex</code></td>\n<td>14</td>\n<td><code>df_to_latex</code></td>\n<td>2026-09-23</td>\n<td><strong>current</strong>: N and rate, all and Russia; CIs not recomputed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6</td>\n<td><code>descriptives/occupation/occupation_qualifier.tex</code></td>\n<td>15</td>\n<td><code>df_to_latex</code></td>\n<td>2026-09-23</td>\n<td>the two <code>zámečník</code> rows equal (1,205 / 2.82; 2,155 / 4.78); other 15 rows not recomputed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>7</td>\n<td><code>descriptives/occupation/desertion_by_hisclass_robustness.tex</code></td>\n<td>16</td>\n<td><code>df_to_latex</code></td>\n<td>2026-09-23</td>\n<td><strong>current</strong>: both rate columns and N exact equal</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>8</td>\n<td><code>descriptives_habsburg/causes/cause_breakdown.tex</code></td>\n<td>20</td>\n<td><code>df_to_latex</code></td>\n<td>2026-06-29</td>\n<td><strong>current</strong>: 7 counts equal</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>9</td>\n<td><code>descriptives_habsburg/theater/theatre_composition.tex</code></td>\n<td>21</td>\n<td><code>df_to_latex</code></td>\n<td>2026-06-29</td>\n<td><strong>current</strong>: 8 counts equal</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>10</td>\n<td><code>descriptives_habsburg/data_quality/top_ah_units.tex</code></td>\n<td>23</td>\n<td><code>df_to_latex</code></td>\n<td>2026-06-14</td>\n<td>top 5 equal; rows 6–20 not recomputed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>11</td>\n<td><code>descriptives_habsburg/data_quality/birth_land.tex</code></td>\n<td>24</td>\n<td><code>df_to_latex</code></td>\n<td>2026-09-23</td>\n<td><strong>STALE</strong>: prints Czech lands 122,552 / missing 40,784; today 122,556 / 40,780</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>12</td>\n<td><code>descriptives_habsburg/data_quality/note_signals.tex</code></td>\n<td>25</td>\n<td><code>df_to_latex</code></td>\n<td>2026-09-23</td>\n<td><strong>current</strong>: 966 / 19,247 / 12,375 / 992</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>13</td>\n<td><code>descriptives_habsburg/data_quality/summary.tex</code></td>\n<td>26</td>\n<td><code>summary_table</code></td>\n<td>2026-09-23</td>\n<td><strong>current</strong>: all 7 rows (N, mean, sd, min, max) equal</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>14</td>\n<td><code>linkage/overlap_summary.tex</code></td>\n<td>28</td>\n<td><code>df_to_latex</code></td>\n<td>2026-09-23</td>\n<td><strong>current</strong>: 1,201 / 139 / 1,340</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p>The file times (2026-06-14 to 2026-09-23) predate today's <code>data/final</code>, yet 12 of the 14\ntables match it in every number checked. Only <code>birth_land.tex</code> changed with the 2026-11-05\nrebuild. File time is not evidence of staleness here (see B5).</p>\n<p><strong>Presentation defect, not a staleness one.</strong> <code>cause_breakdown</code>, <code>theatre_composition</code>,\n<code>birth_land</code> and <code>note_signals</code> round the share to one decimal (<code>.round(1)</code>), then print it\nwith two. Nonzero counts therefore appear as <code>0.00</code> (53 executions, 90 Hungary births), and\n<code>15.1</code> shows as <code>15.10</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Fix.</strong> Re-run notebook 03 after the A2 rebuild. Format shares once, at the precision\nprinted.</p>\n<h3 id=\"notebook-01-2-tables-missing_table\">Notebook 01 (2 tables, <code>missing_table</code>)</h3>\n<p><code>descriptives/data_quality/missing_rates.tex</code> (cell 25) and\n<code>descriptives_habsburg/data_quality/missing_rates.tex</code> (cell 26), both 2026-10-15. They read\n<code>data/raw</code>, not <code>data/final</code>. <strong>Not recomputed.</strong> One cross-check: the legionnaire table's\n\"Political affiliation 70.2 %\" equals <code>CLAUDE.md</code>'s 93,377 / 132,993 blank.</p>\n<h3 id=\"orphans-3-tables\">Orphans (3 tables)</h3>\n<p><code>sample/sample_waterfall.tex</code>, <code>sample/sample_desertion_cut.tex</code>,\n<code>sample/desertion_by_rankreset.tex</code> (2026-07-14). No writer exists (B4); already open in\n<code>ROADMAP.md:29</code>.</p>\n<h3 id=\"the-register-and-the-recheck\">The register and the recheck</h3>\n<p><strong>No LaTeX table exists or is written.</strong> There is no <code>df_to_latex</code> call and no <code>.tex</code> output\npath in <code>utils/recheck/</code>, <code>utils/lexikon_1910/</code>, <code>utils/docs/</code>, <code>utils/reference_tools/</code>, or\nnotebooks 15, 15b, 16 and 17 (<code>grep -rlE 'df_to_latex|\\.tex\"'</code>). The register's accuracy\nfigures (<a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-127\">D-127</a>, <a class=\"dref\" href=\"#decisions-d-226\">D-226</a>) exist only as score JSON and on the docs site.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"audit-repo-not-checked\">Not checked</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Bit-identical regeneration of the run crops.</li>\n<li>A cache-only replay of notebooks 15 → 15b → 17.</li>\n<li>The size of the German reply cache (<code>…/heavyhorse6/de/</code>).</li>\n<li><code>output/publish/</code>.</li>\n<li>The 28 figures.</li>\n<li>The docs site.</li>\n<li>Notebook 01's tables against <code>data/raw</code>.</li>\n<li>Every provider's current licence terms and the AEA/QJE policy text (not re-fetched).</li>\n<li>Whether <code>D:\\Users_Data\\thaufer</code> is backed up.</li>\n<li>The number of crosswalk tie-breaks that A2 changes.</li>\n</ul></div>");
